#META 2026-11-24^November 20, 2026^May 2026 to October 2026 ¶ #NOTE 0~USCIS Service Center Operations (SCOPS) prioritizes processing of Form I-140, Immigrant Petition for Alien Workers, when the Department of State Visa Bulletin shows an immigrant visa is available. The Visa Bulletin, published monthly, lists available immigrant visas by priority date. We use the visa bulletin to determine the current visa categories and priority dates. SCOPS has prioritized our adjudications so we can focus on cases with visas available and can move related Applications to Register Permanent Residence or Adjust Status (Form I-485) to the National Benefits Center. This prioritization supports the USCIS-wide effort to use all employment-based visas available during the fiscal year. It does not affect premium processed petitions, which we will manage in the associated time frame for premium processing service. ¶ #OFF SCD~Service Center Operations (SCOPS) ¶ #OFF FOD~All Field Offices ¶ @I-140^136A-E11^Extraordinary ability (E11)|SCD:36:2023-10-25:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-E12^Outstanding professor or researcher (E12)|SCD:15:2025-03-27:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-E13^Multinational executive or manager (E13)|SCD:29.5:2024-04-27:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-E21^Advanced degree or exceptional ability (E21)|SCD:3.5:2026-05-07:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-E31^Skilled worker or professional (E31; E32)|SCD:4.5:2026-03-22:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-EW3^Unskilled worker (EW3)|SCD:8.5:2025-07-17:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-NIW^Advanced degree or exceptional ability requesting a National Interest Waiver (NIW)|SCD:32:2023-12-02:0 ¶ @I-140^136A-NUR^Schedule A Nurses|SCD:26.5:2024-07-27:0 ¶ @I-131^141A-RT^Re-entry permit or refugee travel document|SCD:16.5:2025-02-24:- ¶ @I-131^141B-OTH^Advance parole|SCD:16:2025-03-18:- ¶ @I-751^148A^Removal of lawful permanent resident conditions (spouses of U.S. citizens and lawful permanent residents)|FOD:35:2022-08-02:- ¶ @I-90^140A^Initial issuance or replacement|SCD:6.5:2026-02-01:- ¶ @I-90^140B^10-year renewal|SCD:10:2025-11-06: